1
00:00:00,839 --> 00:00:02,049
(Leonard:)Yes.

2
00:00:02,215 --> 00:00:04,255
(Sheldon:)Then I suppose
you could have agreed to go.

3
00:00:04,426 --> 00:00:06,926
(Leonard:)And what would I have said afterwards?

4
00:00:07,095 --> 00:00:09,175
(Sheldon:)I would suggest something
to the effect of:

5
00:00:09,347 --> 00:00:12,727
"Singing is neither an appropriate vocation
nor avocation for you...

6
00:00:12,892 --> 00:00:16,102
...and if you disagree, I recommend
a CAT scan to look for a tumor...

7
00:00:16,271 --> 00:00:19,811
(Sheldon:)...pressing on the cognitive
processing centers of your brain."

8
00:00:21,109 --> 00:00:22,239
(Leonard:)I couldn't say that.

9
00:00:22,402 --> 00:00:26,702
I would have to say, "You were terrific
and I can't wait to hear you sing again."

10
00:00:27,324 --> 00:00:29,034
(Penny:)Why?

11
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:30,990
(Leonard:)It's the social protocol.

12
00:00:31,161 --> 00:00:32,201
(Leonard:)It's what you do...

13
00:00:32,370 --> 00:00:35,750
(Leonard:)...when you have a friend who's proud
of something they really suck at.

14
00:00:36,750 --> 00:00:38,210
(Sheldon:)I was not aware of that.

15
00:00:38,376 --> 00:00:40,966
- Well, now you are.
- Oh, all right.

16
00:00:41,129 --> 00:00:42,629
- Leonard?
- Yes?

17
00:00:42,797 --> 00:00:46,677
(Sheldon:)When we played chess earlier, you were
terrific, and I can't wait to play you again.

18
00:00:46,843 --> 00:00:48,383
Good night.

19
00:00:51,639 --> 00:00:52,679
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

20
00:00:52,849 --> 00:00:54,429
SHELDON:
Leonard? Leonard?

21
00:00:54,601 --> 00:00:56,981
Leonard? Leonard?

22
00:00:57,145 --> 00:01:00,355
(Leonard:)This would be so much easier
if I were a violent sociopath.

